From e04f85af30581fb72fb2929b3ff36fddbc15860d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:05:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Name mapper: one socket per bridge; traffic live file fast
 only while watched (102.8 line)

- rdnsmapd opens one packet socket per LAN bridge and one for lo, each bound to its interface,
  rechecked every 30 s, instead of one socket on every interface.
- rtrafd rewrites its live file ten times a second only while the Traffic page or the dashboard
  has asked for it in the last 15 s, else once a second.
- System Information reads the connection table directly instead of copying it to a fixed /tmp
  file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
